      "location": "Proof step 1.2",
      "defect": "unlicensed-inference",
      "evidence": "The proof says, “For each $v>S$ ... hence $$\\left|\\frac{F(v)}v\\right|\\le\\frac{|F(S)|}{v}+\\varepsilon\\frac{v-S}{v}.$$” Its stated choice only requires $S\\ge v_0$, so it does not ensure $v>0$ for every $v>S$; the quotient is undefined at $v=0$, and division can reverse the bound when $v<0$. Restricting to sufficiently large $v>\\max(S,0)$ repairs this immediately; the claimed limit is unaffected.",
